1:["$","div",null,{"className":"blog-shell","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"blog-header","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"/","className":"wordmark","aria-label":"Wen Reloz, home","children":["wr",["$","span",null,{"children":"."}]]}],["$","nav",null,{"aria-label":"Primary navigation","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"/","children":"PORTFOLIO"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"/"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"/blog","children":"BLOG"}]]}]]}],["$","main",null,{"className":"article-shell","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"/blog","className":"back-link","children":[["$","$Ld",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":[["path",{"d":"m12 19-7-7 7-7","key":"1l729n"}],["path",{"d":"M19 12H5","key":"x3x0zl"}]],"className":"lucide-arrow-left","size":15}]," All articles"]}],["$","article",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"short-rule"}]," ","SOFTWARE / PRACTICE"]}],["$","h1",null,{"children":["Why I Still Start with the Problem",["$","span",null,{"children":"."}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"article-lede","children":"A practical note about understanding the real problem before choosing tools and writing code."}],"$undefined",["$","div",null,{"className":"article-rule"}],[["$","div","The fastest way to build the wrong thing is to start with the solution. Before I choose a framework, design a database, or write an endpoint, I want to understand the problem in plain language.",{"children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"The fastest way to build the wrong thing is to start with the solution. Before I choose a framework, design a database, or write an endpoint, I want to understand the problem in plain language."}],"$undefined"]}],["$","div","That means asking who experiences the problem, what they do today, where the process breaks down, and what a useful outcome actually looks like. Those questions often reveal that the first technical idea is larger or more complicated than the work requires.",{"children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"That means asking who experiences the problem, what they do today, where the process breaks down, and what a useful outcome actually looks like. Those questions often reveal that the first technical idea is larger or more complicated than the work requires."}],"$undefined"]}],["$","div","Once the problem is clear, technical decisions become easier to explain. Architecture has a reason. A feature has a measurable purpose. Testing reflects the workflow people depend on instead of only confirming that the code runs.",{"children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Once the problem is clear, technical decisions become easier to explain. Architecture has a reason. A feature has a measurable purpose. Testing reflects the workflow people depend on instead of only confirming that the code runs."}],"$undefined"]}],["$","div","Good engineering is not measured by how much technology goes into a system. It is measured by how reliably the system solves the problem it was built for.",{"children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"Good engineering is not measured by how much technology goes into a system. It is measured by how reliably the system solves the problem it was built for."}],"$undefined"]}]],"$undefined"]}],["$","aside",null,{"className":"article-end","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"END OF ARTICLE"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/wen-reloz-767671206/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","children":["Continue the conversation ",["$","$Ld",null,{"ref":"$undefined","iconNode":[["path",{"d":"M7 7h10v10","key":"1tivn9"}],["path",{"d":"M7 17 17 7","key":"1vkiza"}]],"className":"lucide-arrow-up-right","size":16}]]}]]}]]}],["$","footer",null,{"className":"blog-footer","children":["© ",2026," Wen Reloz ",["$","span",null,{"children":"Always learning. Sometimes writing."}]]}]]}]
